Z||000025||FieroKyle||10-31-2001||11:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88 Fiero:<BR><B>I think it was last month when I was watching Motor Trend... They are showing the new Trucks that are coming out...This particular GMC or Chevy Truck will have the ability to shut off half of the cylinders in a V8 version so it could save gas and the other half would come alive if you step on the gas for towing heavy stuffs... Does anyone seen it????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah I saw that article too. The problem with the Caddy's in the 80's is that you can feel it when the engine shut off and turned on cylinders. They really vibrated when they had 6 turning. I guess the new Chevy's, performance or feeling the engine change change is totally unaffected and you couldn't tell the difference. Its pretty neat really.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
